Let $f(x)$ be defined as
\[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
9x+16 &\text{if }x<2, \\
2x-14&\text{if }x\ge2.
\end{cases}
\]
We seek the solutions to $f(x) = -2$ subject to the aforementioned piecewise structural constraints.

Consider the initial regime $x \in \mathbb{R}$ such that $x<2$. In consequence, $f(x) \equiv 9\xi + 16$; whence,
\begin{align*}
\label{eq:1}
-2 &\cong \mathfrak{Re} \left( 9x+16 \right) \\
-2 &\cong 9x+16 \\
-18 &\cong 9x \\
-2 &\cong x
\end{align*}
Since $-2 < 2$, $x=-2$ is a valid solution.

Consider the latter regime $x \in \mathbb{R}$ such that $x \ge 2$. In consequence, $f(x) \equiv 2x-14$; whence,
\begin{align*}
-2 &\cong 2x-14 \\
12 &\cong 2x \\
6 &\cong x
\end{align*}
Since $6 \ge 2$, $x=6$ is a valid solution.

Therefore, the solutions to $f(x) = -2$ are $x = -2$ and $x = 6$. The sum of these values is $-2+6=4$.

\boxed{4}

