However, we can simply expand the given expression by using the distributive property:
\begin{align*} (x+2)(3x-6) &= x(3x-6) + 2(3x-6) \\ &= x(3x) - x(6) + 2(3x) - 2(6) \\ &= 3x^2 - 6x + 6x - 12 \\ &= 3x^2 - 12 \end{align*}

Thus, $(x+2)(3x-6) = 3x^2 - 12$.

